{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ByG8EgtGaJQYLFarHBhnuG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for every \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier definition. Let me go through each planned experiment and create predictions with rationales.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments:\n- plan_010: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n- plan_011: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n- plan_012: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n- plan_013: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n\n\n- plan_020: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n- plan_021: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n- plan_022: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n- plan_023: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n- plan_030: RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\n- plan_031: Actor entropy analysis\n- plan_032: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n- plan_033: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n- plan_040\n\n: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n\nI need to focus on the planned experiments: plan_010 through plan_013, plan_020 through plan_023, plan_030 through plan_033, and plan_040. For the median tier, I'm seeing that Walker Walk shows the causal chain holds but Cheetah Run's mechanism weakens with multi-seed variance, so I should adjust the claim from \"root cause\" to \"primary contributing factor\" and define the key metrics ranges for each prediction.\n\nFor Walker Walk, I'm expecting the 008d collapse to replicate in 2 out of 3 seeds with one showing degradation but not full collapse, 008f staying stable in 2 out of 3 seeds, and 008a showing V-recovery in 2 out of 3 seeds with one only plateauing. With Cheetah Run, the trained dt_emb should degrade but less dramatically than Walker Walk with normalized v/e ratios between 1.2-1.5x, untrained dt_emb provides some protection though the gap narrows, and the best dt2 configuration reaches 50-75% of baseline performance. For the analysis experiments, I'm looking at RSSM reconstruction loss showing environment-dependent gaps and actor entropy displaying some divergence patterns.\n\nNow I'm examining the value distribution overestimation patterns and dt_embedding cosine similarity metrics to complete the analysis picture.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":32329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08c3fe0c-daed-4e48-875d-eda416d545f0","uuid":"fba5351f-642f-44f9-9eb1-a54867586e3a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ByG8EgtGaJQYLFarHBhnuG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  因果诊断在 Walker Walk 仍成立但需加 nuance。标题用 \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"。\n  C2 措辞从 \"root cause\" 调为 \"primary contributing factor in Walker Walk\"。\n  Cheetah Run 引入 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 讨论——RSSM prediction error 的环境依赖性调节 dt_embedding 危害程度。\n  v/e overshoot ratio 从硬规则降为启发式。Discussion 增加 \"boundary conditions\" 分析。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Walker Walk multi-seed replication (plans 010–013)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration curves\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 610\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 890\n      seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.255\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.42\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.67\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 580\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 870\n      seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 920\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.64\n      cross_seed_mean_last10: 935\n      cross_seed_std_last10: 15\n      cross_seed_ve_stable_range: \"67-74%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance 较小。\n      Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。\n      这是 median 档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。\n      v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03 偏移，\n      这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_ve, seed1_ve, seed2_ve, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 0.087, 0.095, 0.08, 0.087, 0.006]\n          - [35K, 0.241, 0.255, 0.22, 0.239, 0.014]\n          - [55K, 0.404, 0.42, 0.38, 0.401, 0.016]\n          - [105K, 0.656, 0.67, 0.64, 0.655, 0.012]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed baseline learning curves (eval return vs step), shaded std band. All converge to ~920-950 by 200K.\"\n      - \"3-seed v/e ratio curves overlaid. Near-identical shape, stable from 135K+.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。\n      v/e stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。\n      这意味着 >1.5x normalized v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.45\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.72\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.76\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 2.17\n      seed1_verdict: COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 180\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 170\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 162\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.35\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.55\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.59\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.66\n      seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\n      collapse_replication_count: 2  # seed 0 + seed 1 collapse; seed 2 degradation only\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_45K: 143\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation 不 collapse。\n      Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。\n      Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。\n      Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x），\n      但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e 加速率较低。\n      可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation，\n      使 value overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害，\n      但 variance 阻止了 \"100% collapse\" 的强结论，需用 \"primary contributing factor\" 措辞。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 167, 155, 180, 1.78, 1.73, 1.52]\n          - [35K, 146, 138, 170, 1.71, 1.76, 1.59]\n          - [45K, 141, 125, 162, 2.09, 2.17, 1.66]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008d learning curves. Seed 0,1 show clear collapse; seed 2 shows degradation with slower decline.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e trajectories. All >1.5x, but seed 2 slope shallower.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x），\n      1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological zone 但增速慢）。\n      这支持 \"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\" 而非 \"deterministic root cause\"。\n      normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 185\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 215\n      seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 0.98\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.78\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.70\n      seed1_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 175\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 190\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed2_normalized_ve_25K: 1.08\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.85\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      seed2_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n      stable_replication_count: 3  # all 3 seeds stable\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 207\n      cross_seed_nve_range_55K: \"0.70-0.82\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。\n      Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve 1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。\n      移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息，\n      因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。\n      Eval performance 受限于 H=8 + subsample ON（学习信号减少），\n      停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。\n      3/3 seeds stable 是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \"移除有害因素\" 的实验，\n      variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse 的二分上。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f stability replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 197, 185, 175, 1.02, 0.98, 1.08]\n          - [35K, 207, 195, 190, 0.73, 0.78, 0.85]\n          - [55K, 210, 215, 200, 0.68, 0.70, 0.82]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008f learning curves. All slowly increasing, no collapse. Clear contrast with 008d.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e: all converge below 1.0x by 35K, confirming dt_embedding removal eliminates delusional critic.\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。\n      因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的 subsample ON + H=8 条件下，\n      唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。\n      即使 008d seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x）\n      与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确 gap。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 510\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 550\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.88\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n      seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed1_verdict: V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 460\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 530\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 520\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 580\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.95\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0  # plateau, no clear V pattern\n      seed2_verdict: PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\n      recovery_replication_count: 2  # seed 0 + seed 1 show V-recovery; seed 2 plateau\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 693\n      multiseed_mean_105K_range: \"580-778\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不 recover。\n      Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。\n      Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation，\n      允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。\n      Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse），\n      但 eval return 在 530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。\n      可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable 的 policy，\n      value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n      关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x，\n      protective effect 是 robust 的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。\n      cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3 ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 488, 510, 460, 0.93, 0.88, 0.95]\n          - [65K, 608, 580, 530, 0.66, 0.72, 0.80]\n          - [85K, 584, 550, 520, 0.68, 0.71, 0.76]\n          - [105K, 778, 720, 580, 0.59, 0.65, 0.78]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008a learning curves. Seed 0,1 show V-shaped recoveries; seed 2 plateaus at ~530 without collapse.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e: all consistently <1.0x, confirming structural value suppression across seeds.\"\n    analysis: >\n      V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \"V-shaped recovery is a signature\" \n      调整为 \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e, \n      with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\"。\n      核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds robust。\n      V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence 而非 strong claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run cross-environment (plans 020–023)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 450\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 680\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 430\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 660\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 760\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 470\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 700\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 800\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.19\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.35\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.55\n      ve_stable_range: \"58-65%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain），\n      RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。\n      v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 不同。\n      3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local optima）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 220, 25, 0.10, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 310, 20, 0.19, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 450, 20, 0.35, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 680, 20, 0.55, 0.04]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah Run 3-seed baseline with shaded std. Slower initial learning than Walker, smooth convergence.\"\n      - \"Cheetah v/e calibration curve. Same monotonic rise shape as Walker but lower asymptote (~60% vs ~70%).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%），\n      这将影响 normalized v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。\n      需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用 Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 160\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 200\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 180\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.35\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.45\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.50\n      seed0_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 220\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.25\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.38\n      seed1_verdict: DEGRADATION_MILD\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 185\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 165\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.40\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n      seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 183\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.35  # mean across seeds, peak 1.52\n      collapse_count: 0  # no full collapse, only degradation\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: -59%\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker 剧烈\n      （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。\n      机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。\n      因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。\n      normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。\n      Eval return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。\n      这产生了关键的 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 叙事：\n      相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。\n      从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens* 而非 weakens 因果解释——\n      因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\"\n        columns: [env, step, mean_eval, mean_nve, walker_008d_nve, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [Cheetah, 25K, 170, 1.20, 1.78, \"-0.58x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 202, 1.33, 1.71, \"-0.38x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 45K, 195, 1.42, 2.09, \"-0.67x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 183, 1.47, \"N/A (collapsed)\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline. Degradation visible but no sharp collapse.\"\n      - \"Cross-environment normalized v/e comparison: Walker 008d (accelerating >2.0x) vs Cheetah (plateau ~1.3-1.5x).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \"attenuated Walker\" 而非 \"clean replication\"。\n      这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。\n      需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。\n      Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。\n      Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。\n      v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.82\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.75\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 210\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.80\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 230\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 220\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.76\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve: 0.76\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: -51%\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+37 (220 vs 183)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap 较 Walker 小。\n      在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。\n      在 Cheetah 中，gap 缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。\n      Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median 档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。\n      因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 较小。\n      这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 183, 1.47, \"degradation (no collapse)\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 220, 0.76, \"no degradation\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 450, \"1.0 (reference)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah causal comparison: trained dt_emb (declining, elevated nve) vs dt_embed_dim=0 (stable, suppressed nve).\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance），\n      但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \"boundary conditions\" section 的核心数据：\n      当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76 落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 380\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 550\n      seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 520\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 490\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline_pct_105K: -24%\n      v_recovery_count: \"1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\"\n      cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct: 67%  # 520/780\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。\n      Walker 中 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。\n      原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 → \n      untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" 相对 margin 也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。\n      V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有 1/3 seeds 出现，\n      因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n      cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0, seed1, seed2, mean, nve_mean]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 380, 360, 350, 363, 0.88]\n          - [75K, 420, 440, 410, 423, 0.82]\n          - [105K, 550, 520, 490, 520, 0.77]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves. Slow monotonic improvement, fewer oscillations than Walker.\"\n      - \"Cross-environment untrained dt_emb comparison: Walker shows V-recovery, Cheetah shows plateau-rise.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse, nve<1.0x）\n      但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致：\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。\n      论文中可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism is general, \n      but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Diagnostic / analysis experiments (plans 030–033)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from existing trained models across both environments\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 4.2\n      walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 6.8\n      walker_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.62\n      cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 3.9\n      cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 5.1\n      cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.31\n      walker_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.08\n      walker_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.25\n      cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.06\n      cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.12\n      cross_env_recon_gap_ratio: 1.24  # walker_ratio / cheetah_ratio\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。\n      Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时\n      RSSM 需要 \"想象\" 中间状态，reconstruction loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换），\n      dt=2 的 prediction 误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。\n      这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker 导致 collapse \n      而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic gradient → 更快 collapse。\n      Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio），\n      因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment\"\n        columns: [environment, loss_dt1, loss_dt2, ratio, reward_err_dt1, reward_err_dt2, reward_ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, 4.2, 6.8, 1.62, 0.08, 0.25, 3.13]\n          - [Cheetah Run, 3.9, 5.1, 1.31, 0.06, 0.12, 2.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=1 vs dt=2 for both environments. Walker gap visibly larger.\"\n      - \"Scatter: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio (x) vs peak normalized v/e in trained dt_emb config (y). Two points but on the expected trend line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_030 提供了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。\n      Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x），\n      这与 Walker 中 trained dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。\n      但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。\n      论文中应呈现为 \"consistent with the hypothesis\" 而非 \"proves\"。\n      如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs collapsed (006/008d) configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.8\n      walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.1\n      walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.5\n      walker_008d_entropy_trend: increasing\n      walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.9\n      walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.2\n      walker_006_entropy_trend: sharply_increasing\n      walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.2\n      walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.8\n      walker_008a_entropy_trend: stable_to_decreasing\n      walker_008f_entropy_35K: 3.5\n      walker_008f_entropy_trend: stable\n      walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 3.0\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.5\n      walker_baseline_entropy_trend: decreasing\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。\n      当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference → entropy 升高。\n      预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion），\n      而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。\n      这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check：\n      如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则 C2 的 \"delusional critic → actor degradation\" 链需要修正。\n      Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy trajectories\"\n        columns: [config, entropy_25K, entropy_35K, entropy_45K, entropy_55K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 3.2, 3.0, 2.9, 2.8, decreasing]\n          - [008d (collapse), 3.8, 4.1, 4.5, \"—\", increasing]\n          - [006 (collapse), 3.5, 3.9, 4.2, 5.2, sharply increasing]\n          - [008a (V-recovery), 3.3, 3.1, 3.0, 3.2, stable]\n          - [008f (stable), 3.4, 3.5, 3.3, \"—\", stable]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward, healthy configs converge downward. Clear separation after 25K.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n      Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 一致。\n      在 paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.35\n      walker_008d_value_bias: \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\"\n      walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.1  # V(s) variance / MC return variance\n      walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.72\n      walker_008a_value_bias: \"+8% (mild overestimation)\"\n      walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.2\n      walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.85\n      walker_baseline_value_bias: \"+5%\"\n      walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.1\n      walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.68\n      walker_008f_value_bias: \"+10%\"\n      walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。\n      008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x），\n      (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。\n      这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\" 的 distributional fingerprint。\n      008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias 小、相关性高。\n      Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline\n      （因为 dt=2 imagination 本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Value calibration summary\"\n        columns: [config, correlation, bias_pct, variance_ratio, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 0.85, \"+5%\", 1.1, calibrated]\n          - [008a (untrained), 0.72, \"+8%\", 1.2, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [008f (no dt_emb), 0.68, \"+10%\", 1.3, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [008d (trained), 0.35, \"+45%\", 2.1, delusional]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 scatter plot grid: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d. Each with y=x line and regression fit.\"\n      - \"Histogram: value prediction error distribution (V(s) - MC) for each config. 008d shows heavy right tail.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration 证据。\n      008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——value function 的预测\n      与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。\n      这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text 中给一段或一个 figure。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_5K: 0.92\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.75\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.42\n      cosine_sim_55K: 0.28\n      embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.2\n      embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.8\n      embedding_divergence_onset: \"~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。\n      早期（<10K）dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。\n      15-25K 时 embedding 开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7），\n      这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。\n      这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding 的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。\n      dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征，\n      可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（但实际是虚假的）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding evolution during training\"\n        columns: [step, cosine_sim, norm_dt1, norm_dt2, nve_at_step]\n        rows:\n          - [5K, 0.92, 0.8, 0.9, \"~1.0x\"]\n          - [15K, 0.75, 1.0, 1.4, \"~1.2x\"]\n          - [25K, 0.55, 1.1, 2.1, \"~1.5x\"]\n          - [35K, 0.42, 1.2, 2.8, \"~1.7x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: cosine similarity (decreasing) and normalized v/e (increasing) vs training step. Divergence onset co-occurs.\"\n      - \"2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]. dt=1 and dt=2 clusters separate over training.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation → collapse。\n      这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence，\n      但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline figure。\n      如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Third environment validation (plan 040)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_asymptotic: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_peak: 120\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse: \"partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\"\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 105\n      no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.85\n      baseline_ve_stable: \"55-62%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah ~780）。\n      RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间\n      （有 hopping contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。\n      Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.5x），\n      1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。\n      dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。\n      但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 → \n      结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。\n      P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop results summary\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_55K, mean_nve_55K, collapse_fraction]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 180, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 95, 1.55, \"1/3\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 105, 0.85, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-environment summary: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio vs peak normalized v/e. Three points showing positive trend.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。\n      如果 RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测），\n      且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上——\n      这将 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。\n      但 P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。\n      Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion 中的 \"boundary conditions\" 段覆盖。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":32329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08c3fe0c-daed-4e48-875d-eda416d545f0","uuid":"784c50cf-476e-4824-ac3f-69e5a8627846"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":243420,"duration_api_ms":244651,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  因果诊断在 Walker Walk 仍成立但需加 nuance。标题用 \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"。\n  C2 措辞从 \"root cause\" 调为 \"primary contributing factor in Walker Walk\"。\n  Cheetah Run 引入 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 讨论——RSSM prediction error 的环境依赖性调节 dt_embedding 危害程度。\n  v/e overshoot ratio 从硬规则降为启发式。Discussion 增加 \"boundary conditions\" 分析。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Walker Walk multi-seed replication (plans 010–013)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration curves\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 610\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 890\n      seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.255\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.42\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.67\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 580\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 870\n      seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 920\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.64\n      cross_seed_mean_last10: 935\n      cross_seed_std_last10: 15\n      cross_seed_ve_stable_range: \"67-74%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance 较小。\n      Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。\n      这是 median 档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。\n      v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03 偏移，\n      这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_ve, seed1_ve, seed2_ve, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 0.087, 0.095, 0.08, 0.087, 0.006]\n          - [35K, 0.241, 0.255, 0.22, 0.239, 0.014]\n          - [55K, 0.404, 0.42, 0.38, 0.401, 0.016]\n          - [105K, 0.656, 0.67, 0.64, 0.655, 0.012]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed baseline learning curves (eval return vs step), shaded std band. All converge to ~920-950 by 200K.\"\n      - \"3-seed v/e ratio curves overlaid. Near-identical shape, stable from 135K+.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。\n      v/e stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。\n      这意味着 >1.5x normalized v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.45\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.72\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.76\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 2.17\n      seed1_verdict: COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 180\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 170\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 162\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.35\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.55\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.59\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.66\n      seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\n      collapse_replication_count: 2  # seed 0 + seed 1 collapse; seed 2 degradation only\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_45K: 143\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation 不 collapse。\n      Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。\n      Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。\n      Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x），\n      但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e 加速率较低。\n      可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation，\n      使 value overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害，\n      但 variance 阻止了 \"100% collapse\" 的强结论，需用 \"primary contributing factor\" 措辞。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 167, 155, 180, 1.78, 1.73, 1.52]\n          - [35K, 146, 138, 170, 1.71, 1.76, 1.59]\n          - [45K, 141, 125, 162, 2.09, 2.17, 1.66]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008d learning curves. Seed 0,1 show clear collapse; seed 2 shows degradation with slower decline.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e trajectories. All >1.5x, but seed 2 slope shallower.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x），\n      1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological zone 但增速慢）。\n      这支持 \"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\" 而非 \"deterministic root cause\"。\n      normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 185\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 215\n      seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 0.98\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.78\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.70\n      seed1_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 175\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 190\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed2_normalized_ve_25K: 1.08\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.85\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      seed2_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n      stable_replication_count: 3  # all 3 seeds stable\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 207\n      cross_seed_nve_range_55K: \"0.70-0.82\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。\n      Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve 1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。\n      移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息，\n      因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。\n      Eval performance 受限于 H=8 + subsample ON（学习信号减少），\n      停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。\n      3/3 seeds stable 是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \"移除有害因素\" 的实验，\n      variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse 的二分上。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f stability replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 197, 185, 175, 1.02, 0.98, 1.08]\n          - [35K, 207, 195, 190, 0.73, 0.78, 0.85]\n          - [55K, 210, 215, 200, 0.68, 0.70, 0.82]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008f learning curves. All slowly increasing, no collapse. Clear contrast with 008d.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e: all converge below 1.0x by 35K, confirming dt_embedding removal eliminates delusional critic.\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。\n      因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的 subsample ON + H=8 条件下，\n      唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。\n      即使 008d seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x）\n      与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确 gap。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 510\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 550\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.88\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n      seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed1_verdict: V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 460\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 530\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 520\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 580\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.95\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0  # plateau, no clear V pattern\n      seed2_verdict: PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\n      recovery_replication_count: 2  # seed 0 + seed 1 show V-recovery; seed 2 plateau\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 693\n      multiseed_mean_105K_range: \"580-778\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不 recover。\n      Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。\n      Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation，\n      允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。\n      Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse），\n      但 eval return 在 530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。\n      可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable 的 policy，\n      value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n      关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x，\n      protective effect 是 robust 的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。\n      cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3 ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 488, 510, 460, 0.93, 0.88, 0.95]\n          - [65K, 608, 580, 530, 0.66, 0.72, 0.80]\n          - [85K, 584, 550, 520, 0.68, 0.71, 0.76]\n          - [105K, 778, 720, 580, 0.59, 0.65, 0.78]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008a learning curves. Seed 0,1 show V-shaped recoveries; seed 2 plateaus at ~530 without collapse.\"\n      - \"3-seed normalized v/e: all consistently <1.0x, confirming structural value suppression across seeds.\"\n    analysis: >\n      V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \"V-shaped recovery is a signature\" \n      调整为 \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e, \n      with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\"。\n      核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds robust。\n      V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence 而非 strong claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run cross-environment (plans 020–023)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 450\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 680\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 430\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 660\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 760\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 470\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 700\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 800\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.19\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.35\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.55\n      ve_stable_range: \"58-65%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain），\n      RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。\n      v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 不同。\n      3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local optima）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 220, 25, 0.10, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 310, 20, 0.19, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 450, 20, 0.35, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 680, 20, 0.55, 0.04]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah Run 3-seed baseline with shaded std. Slower initial learning than Walker, smooth convergence.\"\n      - \"Cheetah v/e calibration curve. Same monotonic rise shape as Walker but lower asymptote (~60% vs ~70%).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%），\n      这将影响 normalized v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。\n      需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用 Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 160\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 200\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 180\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.35\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.45\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.50\n      seed0_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 220\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.25\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.38\n      seed1_verdict: DEGRADATION_MILD\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 185\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 165\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.40\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n      seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 183\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.35  # mean across seeds, peak 1.52\n      collapse_count: 0  # no full collapse, only degradation\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: -59%\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker 剧烈\n      （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。\n      机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。\n      因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。\n      normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。\n      Eval return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。\n      这产生了关键的 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 叙事：\n      相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。\n      从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens* 而非 weakens 因果解释——\n      因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\"\n        columns: [env, step, mean_eval, mean_nve, walker_008d_nve, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [Cheetah, 25K, 170, 1.20, 1.78, \"-0.58x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 202, 1.33, 1.71, \"-0.38x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 45K, 195, 1.42, 2.09, \"-0.67x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 183, 1.47, \"N/A (collapsed)\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline. Degradation visible but no sharp collapse.\"\n      - \"Cross-environment normalized v/e comparison: Walker 008d (accelerating >2.0x) vs Cheetah (plateau ~1.3-1.5x).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \"attenuated Walker\" 而非 \"clean replication\"。\n      这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。\n      需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。\n      Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。\n      Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。\n      v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.82\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.75\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 210\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.80\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 230\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 220\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.76\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve: 0.76\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: -51%\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+37 (220 vs 183)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap 较 Walker 小。\n      在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。\n      在 Cheetah 中，gap 缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。\n      Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median 档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。\n      因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 较小。\n      这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 183, 1.47, \"degradation (no collapse)\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 220, 0.76, \"no degradation\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 450, \"1.0 (reference)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah causal comparison: trained dt_emb (declining, elevated nve) vs dt_embed_dim=0 (stable, suppressed nve).\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance），\n      但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \"boundary conditions\" section 的核心数据：\n      当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76 落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 380\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 550\n      seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 520\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 490\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline_pct_105K: -24%\n      v_recovery_count: \"1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\"\n      cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct: 67%  # 520/780\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。\n      Walker 中 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。\n      原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 → \n      untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" 相对 margin 也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。\n      V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有 1/3 seeds 出现，\n      因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n      cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0, seed1, seed2, mean, nve_mean]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 380, 360, 350, 363, 0.88]\n          - [75K, 420, 440, 410, 423, 0.82]\n          - [105K, 550, 520, 490, 520, 0.77]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves. Slow monotonic improvement, fewer oscillations than Walker.\"\n      - \"Cross-environment untrained dt_emb comparison: Walker shows V-recovery, Cheetah shows plateau-rise.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse, nve<1.0x）\n      但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致：\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。\n      论文中可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism is general, \n      but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Diagnostic / analysis experiments (plans 030–033)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from existing trained models across both environments\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 4.2\n      walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 6.8\n      walker_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.62\n      cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 3.9\n      cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 5.1\n      cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.31\n      walker_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.08\n      walker_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.25\n      cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.06\n      cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.12\n      cross_env_recon_gap_ratio: 1.24  # walker_ratio / cheetah_ratio\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。\n      Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时\n      RSSM 需要 \"想象\" 中间状态，reconstruction loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换），\n      dt=2 的 prediction 误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。\n      这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker 导致 collapse \n      而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic gradient → 更快 collapse。\n      Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio），\n      因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment\"\n        columns: [environment, loss_dt1, loss_dt2, ratio, reward_err_dt1, reward_err_dt2, reward_ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, 4.2, 6.8, 1.62, 0.08, 0.25, 3.13]\n          - [Cheetah Run, 3.9, 5.1, 1.31, 0.06, 0.12, 2.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=1 vs dt=2 for both environments. Walker gap visibly larger.\"\n      - \"Scatter: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio (x) vs peak normalized v/e in trained dt_emb config (y). Two points but on the expected trend line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_030 提供了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。\n      Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x），\n      这与 Walker 中 trained dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。\n      但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。\n      论文中应呈现为 \"consistent with the hypothesis\" 而非 \"proves\"。\n      如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs collapsed (006/008d) configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.8\n      walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.1\n      walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.5\n      walker_008d_entropy_trend: increasing\n      walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.9\n      walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.2\n      walker_006_entropy_trend: sharply_increasing\n      walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.2\n      walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.8\n      walker_008a_entropy_trend: stable_to_decreasing\n      walker_008f_entropy_35K: 3.5\n      walker_008f_entropy_trend: stable\n      walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 3.0\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.5\n      walker_baseline_entropy_trend: decreasing\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。\n      当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference → entropy 升高。\n      预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion），\n      而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。\n      这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check：\n      如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则 C2 的 \"delusional critic → actor degradation\" 链需要修正。\n      Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy trajectories\"\n        columns: [config, entropy_25K, entropy_35K, entropy_45K, entropy_55K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 3.2, 3.0, 2.9, 2.8, decreasing]\n          - [008d (collapse), 3.8, 4.1, 4.5, \"—\", increasing]\n          - [006 (collapse), 3.5, 3.9, 4.2, 5.2, sharply increasing]\n          - [008a (V-recovery), 3.3, 3.1, 3.0, 3.2, stable]\n          - [008f (stable), 3.4, 3.5, 3.3, \"—\", stable]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward, healthy configs converge downward. Clear separation after 25K.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n      Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 一致。\n      在 paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.35\n      walker_008d_value_bias: \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\"\n      walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.1  # V(s) variance / MC return variance\n      walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.72\n      walker_008a_value_bias: \"+8% (mild overestimation)\"\n      walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.2\n      walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.85\n      walker_baseline_value_bias: \"+5%\"\n      walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.1\n      walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.68\n      walker_008f_value_bias: \"+10%\"\n      walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。\n      008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x），\n      (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。\n      这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\" 的 distributional fingerprint。\n      008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias 小、相关性高。\n      Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline\n      （因为 dt=2 imagination 本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Value calibration summary\"\n        columns: [config, correlation, bias_pct, variance_ratio, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 0.85, \"+5%\", 1.1, calibrated]\n          - [008a (untrained), 0.72, \"+8%\", 1.2, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [008f (no dt_emb), 0.68, \"+10%\", 1.3, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [008d (trained), 0.35, \"+45%\", 2.1, delusional]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 scatter plot grid: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d. Each with y=x line and regression fit.\"\n      - \"Histogram: value prediction error distribution (V(s) - MC) for each config. 008d shows heavy right tail.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration 证据。\n      008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——value function 的预测\n      与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。\n      这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text 中给一段或一个 figure。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_5K: 0.92\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.75\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.42\n      cosine_sim_55K: 0.28\n      embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.2\n      embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.8\n      embedding_divergence_onset: \"~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。\n      早期（<10K）dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。\n      15-25K 时 embedding 开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7），\n      这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。\n      这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding 的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。\n      dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征，\n      可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（但实际是虚假的）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding evolution during training\"\n        columns: [step, cosine_sim, norm_dt1, norm_dt2, nve_at_step]\n        rows:\n          - [5K, 0.92, 0.8, 0.9, \"~1.0x\"]\n          - [15K, 0.75, 1.0, 1.4, \"~1.2x\"]\n          - [25K, 0.55, 1.1, 2.1, \"~1.5x\"]\n          - [35K, 0.42, 1.2, 2.8, \"~1.7x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: cosine similarity (decreasing) and normalized v/e (increasing) vs training step. Divergence onset co-occurs.\"\n      - \"2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]. dt=1 and dt=2 clusters separate over training.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation → collapse。\n      这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence，\n      但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline figure。\n      如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Third environment validation (plan 040)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_asymptotic: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_peak: 120\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse: \"partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\"\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 105\n      no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.85\n      baseline_ve_stable: \"55-62%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah ~780）。\n      RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间\n      （有 hopping contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。\n      Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.5x），\n      1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。\n      dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。\n      但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 → \n      结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。\n      P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop results summary\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_55K, mean_nve_55K, collapse_fraction]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 180, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 95, 1.55, \"1/3\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 105, 0.85, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-environment summary: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio vs peak normalized v/e. Three points showing positive trend.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。\n      如果 RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测），\n      且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上——\n      这将 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。\n      但 P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。\n      Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion 中的 \"boundary conditions\" 段覆盖。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"08c3fe0c-daed-4e48-875d-eda416d545f0","total_cost_usd":0.50228425,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20793,"cache_read_input_tokens":44170,"output_tokens":13386,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":13253,"cache_read_input_tokens":32329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":15448,"outputTokens":26,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.015578,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":13386,"cacheReadInputTokens":44170,"cacheCreationInputTokens":20793,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4867062499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9cf5b2fb-39aa-4ebb-8b4a-367ca3b390fc"}
